WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:02.640
Battery performance changes with temperature.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:06.130
In cold conditions, chemical reactions slow and voltage may sag under load,

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:08.000
reducing usable energy and power.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A battery that appears charged can reach a critical state sooner than expected.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.837
Follow approved guidance for battery temperature and preconditioning.

00:00:14.837 --> 00:00:17.000
Keep batteries in a suitable environment before use,

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
confirm they have reached an acceptable operating condition, and avoid improvised heating.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.931
Plan shorter flights and larger reserves in the cold.

00:00:23.931 --> 00:00:25.620
Heat creates different risks.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.000
High ambient temperature, direct sun, heavy processing, hovering,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.310
and repeated flights can stress batteries, motors, electronics, mobile devices,

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:33.965
and payloads.

00:00:33.965 --> 00:00:39.190
Overheated components may throttle, shut down, age faster, or behave unpredictably.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:41.000
Monitor more than a percentage display.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.475
Observe voltage or cell status when available, temperature warnings, power demand,

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:45.995
battery age, prior damage, swelling,

00:00:45.995 --> 00:00:48.965
and the difference between planned and actual consumption.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:51.190
Treat unexpected behavior as a reason to recover.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.920
Storage and transport affect safety.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:57.420
Protect batteries from physical damage, moisture, extreme temperature, conductive objects,

00:00:57.420 --> 00:00:58.995
and unattended hot vehicles.

00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:01.585
Use approved charging, storage, and retirement practices,

00:01:01.585 --> 00:01:05.260
and isolate questionable batteries according to organizational procedures.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.000
Temperature also affects people and data.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.900
Cold hands, heat stress, screen dimming, condensation,

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:12.260
and sensor drift can degrade decisions.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.190
Environmental planning includes crew endurance and payload quality as well as aircraft

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.000
flight time.
